hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"27674","Haddathana Ya'qub, he said: My father narrated to me from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Salit ibn Ayyub ibn al-Hakam ibn Sulaym narrated to me from his mother, from Salma bint Qays, and she was one of the maternal aunts of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who had prayed toward the two qiblas, and she was one of the women of Banu Adi ibn al-Najjar, she said: I came to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and pledged him among women of the Ansar, and when he stipulated upon us that we shall not associate anything with Allah, nor steal, nor commit adultery, nor kill our children, nor bring slander that we fabricate between our hands and our feet, nor disobey him in what is right, he said: And do not cheat your husbands. She said: So we pledged him, then we left. So I said to a woman among them: Go back and ask the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, what is cheating our husbands? She said: So she asked him, and he said: She takes his wealth and favors another therewith."
